rst solo  assignment however Mort would soon fall  in love with a princess whose life he  was meant to collect and despite his  training he would save her from her fate  which would threaten the balance of the  world since this animated film was set  in a dark and terrifying landscape there  was no way of knowing if the movie would  be a hit or a miss so the project was  soon cancelled the movies directors Ron  Clements and John Musker  went on to create Moana which quickly  became a fan favorite and although we  love Moana we have to admit that morte  sounds intriguing however it might be a  better project for filmmaker Tim Burton  to take on the Shadow King it looks like  it's not the first time Disney took on a  darkly themed project only to drop it  out of the blue after all the shadow  king and Mort seem to have met a similar  fate however when it comes to the shadow  king it sieved  say that it was a bigger disappointment  than any other canceled film after all  it dig it's a boot after costing Disney  fifty million dollars to create the  shadow pink was written by Henry Selick  who famously directed the movie Coraline  Disney backed out of the deal when they  determined that the movie would cost too  much to make the shadow King was about a  New York orphan named hat he had long  and strange fingers that derived from a  cruel world  his deprivation often caused him to be  alienated which led him to become lonely  and sad he would soon meet a living  shadow girl who would go on to teach him  that his bizarre fingers cast beautiful  shadows however they could also be used  as shadowy weapons although this movie  is different and entertaining the shadow  monster was terrifying and could  potentially scare children  after all he wanted to beast on a little  boy which is uh absolutely horrifying  knowing this we're not surprised that  Disney opted out the gremlins most of us  are familiar with the movie gremlins  which was released in 1984 however did  you know th